\section{Step 1:  Find the value of $x$.}
The problem gives us the value of $x$ as $x = -2$.

## Step 2: 
Evaluate $2x^2+3x+4$ by substituting $x = -2$ into the expression.

\begin{align*}
2x^2+3x+4 & = 2(-2)^2 + 3(-2) + 4 \\
& = 2(4) - 6 + 4 \\
& = 8 - 6 + 4 \\
& = 6
\end{align*}

The final answer is: $\boxed{6}$  \boxed{6}

