People  often get confused about which method should be used to solve this type of problem. To make it clearer ,here is a simple example.
 Lets find out the total number of ways to choose 3 boys and 2 girls from a class of 7 boys and 6 girls. 
If the boys can be chosen first and then the girls, then we can just multiply the number of ways to choose 3 boys and 2 girls. That is :
\begin{align*}
\binom{7}{3} \cdot \binom{6}{2} & = \frac{7 \cdot 6 \cdot 5}{3 \cdot 2}  \cdot \frac{6 \cdot 5}{2 \cdot 1}\\
                    & = \frac{7 \cdot 6^2 \cdot 5 \cdot 5}{3 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 1}\\
                    & = \frac{63,000}{12}\\
                    & = \boxed{5,250}. \end{align*}

